21: dateagain:{speaker:'RILEY',note:'AGE 27 · ARCHITECT',scene:'FIRST LIGHT',time:'6:13 AM',chapter:'5 — TOMORROW, TOO',line:'Morning light finds two half-finished cups of tea and a plan for next week. Riley squeezes your hand. “No matter what tonight became, I’m glad I met you.”',ending:'A beginning, not a promise. But beginnings can be beautiful.'},
22: goodnight:{speaker:'RILEY',note:'AGE 27 · ARCHITECT',scene:'FIRST LIGHT',time:'12:26 AM',chapter:'5 — A GOOD NIGHT',line:'You say goodnight with a warm hug and the kind of smile that stays after someone turns away. The city keeps glowing. Somewhere, the next day is already making room for possibility.',ending:'A complete little story. Connection is never owed—and never wasted.'},
